text [0;37mTEST: cpu_dummy_writes_oam\n [0;33mThis program verifies that the\nCPU does 2x writes properly.\nAny read-modify-write opcode\nshould first write the origi-\nnal value; then the calculated\nvalue exactly 1 cycle later.\n\nRequirement: OAM memory reads\nMUST be reliable. This is\noften the case on emulators,\nbut NOT on the real NES.\nNevertheless, this test can be\nused to see if the CPU in the\nemulator is built properly.\n\n [0;37m [0;37mTesting OAM.  The screen will go blank for a moment now.\n [0;37mOK;  [0;37mVerifying opcodes...\n [1;34m0E [1;34m2E [1;34m4E [1;34m6E [1;34mCE [1;34mEE  [1;34m1E [1;34m3E [1;34m5E [1;34m7E [1;34mDE [1;34mFE \n [1;34m0F [1;34m2F [1;34m4F [1;34m6F [1;34mCF [1;34mEF  [1;34m1F [1;34m3F [1;34m5F [1;34m7F [1;34mDF [1;34mFF \n [1;34m03 [1;34m23 [1;34m43 [1;34m63 [1;34mC3 [1;34mE3  [1;34m13 [1;34m33 [1;34m53 [1;34m73 [1;34mD3 [1;34mF3 \n [1;34m1B [1;34m3B [1;34m5B [1;34m7B [1;34mDB [1;34mFB              \n [0;37m\nPassed
